==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fo|non|faðir}}, from {{inh|fo|gem-pro|*fadēr}}, from {{inh|fo|ine-pro|*ph₂tḗr}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|father}}, {{cog|de|Vater}}, {{cog|is|faðir}}, {{cog|no|far}}, {{m|no|fader}}, {{cog|da|far}}, {{m|da|fader}}, {{cog|sv|far}}, {{m|sv|fader}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈfɛaːjɪɹ/|lang=fo}}
* {{rhymes|ɛaːjɪɹ|lang=fo}}

===Noun===
{{fo-noun|m|faðirs|fedrar|22=føður}}

# [[father]]

====Usage notes====
The oblique singular form {{l|fo|føður}} is very rare and limited to poetry.

====Declension====
{{fo-decl-noun-m43|faðir|fedr}}

===Anagrams===
* {{l|fo|farið}}, {{l|fo|friða}}

