==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*fadēr|t=father}}, from {{inh|non|ine-pro|*ph₂tḗr|t=father}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|fæder}}, {{cog|ofs|feder}}, {{cog|osx|fadar}}, {{cog|goh|fater}}, {{cog|got|𐍆𐌰𐌳𐌰𐍂}}.

===Noun===
{{non-noun|m|fǫður|feðr}}

# [[father]]
#*: <font size=4>ᚼᛅᚱᛅᛚᛏᚱ ᛬ ᚴᚢᚾᚢᚴᛦ ᛬ ᛒᛅᚦ ᛬ ᚴᛅᚢᚱᚢᛅ / ᚴᚢᛒᛚ ᛬ ᚦᛅᚢᛋᛁ ᛬ ᛅᚠᛏ ᛬ ᚴᚢᚱᛘ ᚠᛅᚦᚢᚱ ᛋᛁᚾ</font>
#*: ''haraltr : kunukR : baþ : kaurua / kubl : þausi : aft : kurm faþur sin''.
#*: King Haraldr ordered this monument made in memory of Gormr, his father. &mdash; 10th century inscription on the Runestone of Harald Bluetooth, one of the [[w:Jelling stones|Jelling stones]].

